When WikiBinaryManager.ready() rejects after the article has already rendered, WikiEditorProvider posts showWarning and the webview displays it as a non-replacing banner above the article content — never as showError that replaces the rendered page. The type system ensures showWarning is a valid HostMessage variant and is handled in the switch, but nothing enforces the semantic choice of warning vs error in the provider's failure handler or the non-replacing vs content-replacing rendering in the webview handler.
